; The unification itself — ONE DIRECTION ONLY (user ruling: never mint
; gathers from views; the reverse would manufacture a gather plus one
; iota per map entry inside every view's class). An all-iota gather IS a
; view application: out[c] = data[e_0(c), .., e_{r-1}(c)] is exactly the
; index map [e_0 .. e_{r-1}] applied at the coords' common shape. The
; union is at the LOGICAL level; layout tensors keep implementations
; honest (the view rides composed layouts, the materializers require
; injective destinations). Termination: the minted map's entries are
; EXISTING expression classes — no new expressions, no cycle back.
(rule
  (
    (= ?out_logical (LogicalGather ?data_logical ?coordinate_list))
    (coordinate-iota-expressions ?coordinate_list ?entry_expressions)
    (= ?common_shape (coords-common-shape ?coordinate_list))
    ; the minted map's domain tag = the data tensor's own shape
    (= ?data_shape (shape-of ?data_logical))
  )
  (
    (union ?out_logical
      (LogicalIndexMapApply ?data_logical
        (IndexMapLit ?entry_expressions ?data_shape) ?common_shape))
  )
)
